The `[cli-flag]` test passes now. Let me confirm the exact target test and show the fix:

Fixed. The `[cli-flag]` test was failing because `parseFlags` assigned the raw string value (`"8080"`) instead of a number, despite the test expecting `8080`.

**Cause:** `packages/cli/src/flags.js` had an explicit `// TODO: numbers stay strings` — values were never coerced.

**Fix:** Added a `coerce` helper that converts numeric-looking values to `Number`, while leaving non-numeric values and bare flags (`true`) untouched. Empty/whitespace strings are preserved so they don't silently become `0`.

```js
function coerce(value) {
  if (value.trim() === "") return value;
  const num = Number(value);
  return Number.isNaN(num) ? value : num;
}
```

